      "math_academy_id": "q-77321",
      "knowledge_point_id": "f9ccf6b5-e087-5f7b-88e3-3767efbdcc26",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Trigonometric Equations Involving Cosecant with Non-Special Angles",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-\\frac{7}{2}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{2}{7})=(-16.601\\,5…)^{∘}≈-{16.602}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{∘}.$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{16.602}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={343.398}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSo, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={343.398}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={16.602}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={16.602}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989101/assets/c86fca87f7f46c0155be358f377550a4adebf1a2040c874d55c00473766745f5.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{16.602}^{∘} \\\\  & ={196.602}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈343.398\\cdot 196.602=67\\,513\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
      "answer_fields": [
